                  <provenance type="#s"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_122">Canterbury, Kent.
                        Benedictine abbey of St Augustine (originally of St Peter and St Paul).
                        </orgName><p>W. Urry rightly says that this fragment is by 'exactly the same
                        hand' as Canterbury Cathedral Lit. A. 8 (68), q.v.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">This is a bifolium, used as a wrapper for the
                     parish register (starting in 1552) of Elmstone, Kent. In the 1964 edition of
                     MLGB, it was recorded as held at Elmstone Rectory, but by 1985, the Rectory had
                     been sold and was in lay hands, and the fragment could not be traced. Thus, in
                     the 1987 Supplement, it is recorded as untraced.</provenance>
               </history>
